RTU Configuration Record: PC-RTU-01
Alleniom Utilities — SCADA/EMS Engineering · 4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA · (612) 555-0100 · alleniom.com
Doc no. SCADA-PC-RTU-CFG-01  ·  Rev 0  ·  Date 07/08/2025  ·  Owner SCADA/EMS Engineering (Marcus Deele)
Site: Prairie Corridor Business Park PV (PXA-2024-0343), feeder ALN-088. RTU: Kelvraith YOT-8963, firmware 4.12.2.
The site-specific configuration record of TCS-02 §4.2. Issued ahead of installation. To be loaded to the site's RTU at staging, once a set is allocated under OG-17.
Sheets: Settings Export (RTU parameters as exported from the configuration tool), Point Table (DNP3 points to SCADA, in index order).
Prepared: Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineer, 07/08/2025.
[Sheet: Settings Export]
Settings Export
DNP3_OUTSTATION_ADDRESS = 343  |  DNP3_MASTER_ADDRESS = 1
TRANSPORT = DNP3 over TCP/IP  |  LINK = utility cellular, approved carrier (TCS-02 §4.1(c))
SECURE_AUTH = SAv5 enabled  |  UNSOLICITED = classes 1, 2  |  INTEGRITY_POLL = 60 s (master)
VPN = IPsec IKEv2 to the Alleniom SCADA headend, mutual certificates, 13-month validity (TCS-02 §7.3)
PORT_1 = cellular modem  |  PORT_2 = plant LAN 192.168.10.5/24  |  PORT_S1 = RS-485, POI-R1 control NPC-38
MODBUS_CLIENT = enabled, port 2, scan 2 s  |  DEVICE_TABLE = SCADA-PC-RTU-DEV-01
TIME_SOURCE = RTC  |  NTP_SERVER =  |  OPTION_SLOT_1 = serial expansion  |  OPTION_SLOT_2 =
DNP3 time synchronisation from master: disabled
EVENT_BUFFER = 72 h  |  BACKFILL_ON_RESTORE = enabled
CONFIG_VERSION = PC-RTU-01-R0
